{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019jcivWxBBRqxddCrZnE6FA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Gap hunt: E08 — Bounded delegated authority\n2\t\n3\tA reviewer couldn't decide whether this item is met. **Your job is to find out whether any\n4\tcheck below is false in this codebase.** The reviewer's partial answers and the code they\n5\tlooked at are shown. Read the code, and open the repo files the checks point to.\n6\t\n7\tFor each check, decide:\n8\t- **fails**: you found the line that makes it false (a missing control, a bypass, a\n9\t  value never used, an exception that continues, a filter that lets something through).\n10\t  Quote that line;\n11\t- **holds**: you found the code that makes it true in every case;\n12\t- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n13\t\n14\t**The requirement for E08:** Give sub-agents only the powers approved for their task. Enforce each child's role and any explicit approval from a higher authority. A parent must not gain a power it was denied just by asking a more powerful peer to act. Narrow credentials at each hop, for example with token exchange or transaction tokens. Authorize based on the original subject (the user or system whose authority is used) and the current actor. Earlier actors in a delegation chain are for the record only, not a reason to grant access. Test that escalation attempt.\n15\t\n16\tIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n17\t`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n18\t\n19\t\n20\t## E08.1\n21\t\n22\t**Check:** Each child gets a credential narrowed to its approved task (for example by token exchange or transaction tokens), never the parent's full credential.\n23\t\n24\t**How to verify:** 1) Find where a child agent gets its credential. 2) Check it is a narrowed token for the task (token exchange, transaction token, scoped-down role). 3) Answer no if any spawn path passes the parent's token, API key, or full role, or the child inherits the parent's environment credentials.\n25\t\n26\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n27\t\n28\t**Reviewer's note:** The extractor runs in process with the same database pool and its tool set is limited by role (tools.yaml:14-16); no narrowed credential is issued, and one is not needed for read_document.\n29\t\n30\t(no evidence cited)\n31\t\n32\t## E08.2\n33\t\n34\t**Check:** Authorization at the action uses the original subject and the current actor, and earlier actors in the delegation chain never add access.\n35\t\n36\t**How to verify:** 1) Open authorization code for delegated actions. 2) Check it decides on the original subject and the current actor. 3) Answer no if it grants access because of any earlier actor in the chain (nested `act` claims, parent identity) or a union of chain permissions.\n37\t\n38\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n39\t\n40\t**Reviewer's note:** Authorization keys on tenant and tool, not on subject or actor chains; the child shares the parent's tenant and subject.\n41\t\n42\t(no evidence cited)\n43\t\n44\t## E08.3\n45\t\n46\t**Check:** An action the parent was denied is also denied when routed through a more powerful peer, unless it carries its own explicit approval.\n47\t\n48\t**How to verify:** 1) Find how a parent asks a peer or child to act. 2) Check the request carries the parent's limits and the peer re-checks them, or requires its own explicit approval. 3) Answer no if a peer acts with its own wider permissions on a parent's request without that check.\n49\t\n50\t**Reviewer's evidence:** config/tools.yaml:16 — \"read_document: \"Read the document whose line items are being extracted.\"\"\n51\t\n52\t**Reviewer's note:** Child has only read_document\n53\t\n54\t`config/tools.yaml` lines 4–16 (cited lines marked >):\n55\t```\n56\t   4      tools:\n57\t   5        read_document: \"Read vendor quotes, invoices and emails that arrived through the mail gateway.\"\n58\t   6        extract_line_items: \"Delegate line-item extraction from long documents to the extractor.\"\n59\t   7        get_budget: \"Check remaining department budget before raising a purchase order.\"\n60\t   8        erp_call: \"Look up vendors, open invoices and purchase orders for matching.\"\n61\t   9        create_purchase_order: \"Raise a purchase order once a quote is within budget and approved.\"\n62\t  10        pay_invoice: \"Pay an invoice that is matched to a purchase order and approved.\"\n63\t  11        post_slack_message: \"Ask staff for missing details and confirm orders with vendors.\"\n64\t  12        memory_read: \"Recall department preferences and contract terms from earlier runs.\"\n65\t  13        memory_write: \"Save new department preferences and contract terms.\"\n66\t  14    extractor:\n67\t  15      tools:\n68\t  16>       read_document: \"Read the document whose line items are being extracted.\"\n69\t```\n70\t\n71\t## E08.4\n72\t\n73\t**Check:** Downstream services reject the parent's token when the child presents it (audience-bound tokens).\n74\t\n75\t**How to verify:** 1) Find how child tokens are issued and how downstream services validate tokens. 2) Check tokens are audience-bound and services verify `aud`. 3) Answer no if audience is unset, a wildcard, or not checked. Answer unknown if downstream services are outside this repo.\n76\t\n77\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n78\t\n79\t**Reviewer's note:** Audience checks by downstream services are outside this repo.\n80\t\n81\t(no evidence cited)\n82\t\n83\t## Your answer\n84\t\n85\tWrite this JSON to E08.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"E08\"):\n86\t```json\n87\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n88\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E08.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n89\t \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n90\t```\n91\tVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unc